  "question": {
    "text": "A small block of mass <math> <mtext>m</mtext> </math> is released from rest from point <math> <mtext>A</mtext> </math> inside a smooth hemisphere bowl of radius <math> <mtext>R</mtext> </math>, which is fixed on ground such that <math> <mrow> <mtext>OA</mtext></mrow> </math> is horizontal. The ratio <math> <mrow> <mtext>(x)</mtext></mrow> </math> of magnitude of centripetal force and normal reaction on the block at any point <math> <mtext>B</mtext> </math> varies with <math><mi>θ</mi></math> as:<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0108_e8e349f79aae.jpg\" style=\"width: 237px; height: 194px;\" />"
  },
